WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.181 --> 00:00:04.559
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:00:04.559 --> 00:00:06.379
- [Lukas ] There's something magical

00:00:06.379 --> 00:00:10.212
about seeing the arrow
fly and hit the target.

00:00:13.499 --> 00:00:17.742
Archery is difficult enough, you know, on the ground.

00:00:17.742 --> 00:00:19.345
To be on the back of the horse

00:00:19.345 --> 00:00:22.068
and to feel the wind in your face.

00:00:22.068 --> 00:00:25.151
It’s a challenge, and I like challenge.

00:00:28.735 --> 00:00:30.735
My name is Lukas Novotny, and I'm a bowyer

00:00:30.735 --> 00:00:32.905
and horseback archer.
(guitar music)

00:00:32.905 --> 00:00:36.901
What I do here is kind of
a history that's revived

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:39.254
in a sort of modern fashion.

00:00:39.254 --> 00:00:41.593
I don't necessarily like to brag,

00:00:41.593 --> 00:00:45.500
but I'm considered to be
one of the top archers.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.667
I started making bows, uh, just as a hobby.

00:00:50.756 --> 00:00:53.504
And then it kind of just drew me in.

00:00:53.504 --> 00:00:55.518
You wouldn't be interested in a bow unless

00:00:55.518 --> 00:00:56.763
you wanted to shoot it.

00:00:56.763 --> 00:00:58.787
I mean, why would you want to make a bow

00:00:58.787 --> 00:01:03.642
unless you wanted to pull that
string and let the arrow fly?

00:01:03.642 --> 00:01:05.540
To come up with a bow that's perfect,

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:08.305
it's almost next to impossible I suppose,

00:01:08.305 --> 00:01:09.947
but that's where the challenge lies.

00:01:09.947 --> 00:01:11.352
It's like in horseback archery,

00:01:11.352 --> 00:01:13.650
to get a perfect score on a run,

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:17.233
is, you know, that's a feat that
happens once in a while.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.523
(neighs)

00:01:24.732 --> 00:01:28.315
(tense instrumental music)

00:01:30.134 --> 00:01:32.176
Here we have the Hungarian course.

00:01:32.176 --> 00:01:33.893
It's scored by degree of difficulty.

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:38.250
Forward being difficult,
side being the easiest,

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.139
and the back being the most difficult

00:01:40.139 --> 00:01:42.556
and being scored the highest.

00:01:43.409 --> 00:01:46.217
Korean style is basically fairly simple.

00:01:46.217 --> 00:01:49.093
It's a 150 meter track
with five targets spread

00:01:49.093 --> 00:01:50.426
30 meters apart.

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:54.884
The Kabak is a Turkish style.

00:01:56.953 --> 00:01:59.823
Dating back to ancient times.

00:01:59.823 --> 00:02:01.347
It's a pole that's seven meters tall,

00:02:01.347 --> 00:02:03.173
that's what we use as a standard.

00:02:03.173 --> 00:02:06.090
At the top of it you have a target.

00:02:10.792 --> 00:02:13.084
I'm not per se the best archer there is.

00:02:13.084 --> 00:02:15.011
I don't know how it's
possible, how I've managed

00:02:15.011 --> 00:02:17.084
to collect so many medals.

00:02:17.084 --> 00:02:19.373
Maybe it's the saying of
the one man with one eye

00:02:19.373 --> 00:02:23.540
is the king among the blind
or something (laughs).

